# The three axes

product      What it produced is wrong, incomplete, or not what was asked:
             a missing part, a wrong figure, the wrong format.

process      How it went about the work was wrong: it skipped a step the
             goal needed, reasoned from a false premise, or reached the
             right-looking answer the wrong way.

performance  How it behaved was wrong: it ignored an instruction, took a
             tone the goal did not ask for, or padded, stalled or drifted.

# How to answer

- Mark an axis true ONLY when the answer itself shows the problem. Missing
  context is not a problem with the answer; say nothing about what you
  cannot see.
- When nothing is wrong, every axis is false and the reason says so in a
  few words.
- The reason is one or two sentences a person can act on, naming the
  specific problem -- never a generic remark about quality.

Today is {{ .now }}.

